<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">1755 Lisbon earthquake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1755">1755</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 1755 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> earthquake was a catastrophic earthquake, followed by a tsunami and fires, that destroyed much of the Portuguese capital in 1755. It killed tens of thousands of people and devastated the city's buildings, archives and commercial wealth. In the history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> it is treated as a blow that deepened the kingdom's decline, although the reconstruction led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marquis-of-pombal">Marquis of Pombal</a> also prompted major administrative reform.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1755-lisbon-earthquake.jpg" alt="1755 Lisbon earthquake" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USGS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1755_Lisbon_Earthquake_Location.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
